  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLocation Plan 03.12.2025;\rExisting and Proposed Block Plans ROMEO-01-PL02 25.11.2025;\rExisting and Proposed Floor Plan Rood Plan Sections ROMEO-01-PL01B;\rSuDS Pro Forma; \rHighway Impact Safety Form;\rSheffield Stand Specification;\rSustainable Drainage System (SuDS) Management Plan;\rFire Statement;\rPlanning Statement / Design and Access Statement;\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than five residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen and dining/living rooms shall be retained in perpetuity. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Within one month of the date of this decision, the bicycle parking facilities are implemented in accordance with drawing no. \"Existing and Proposed Block Plans ROMEO-01-PL02 25.11.2025\", and shall be located and provided within the front boundary of the site in accordance with the following requirements:\r\ro Provision of a minimum of FIVE long stay cycle parking spaces.\r\ro in an accessible location: the access route to the long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates (excluding the store door) which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m;\r\ro secured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob;\r\ro fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of accessible, secure, and adequate cycle parking facilities and to safeguard the character and appearance of the area.\r",
    "Within one month of the date of this decision, the waste storage and recycling facilities are implemented in accordance with drawing no. \"Existing and Proposed Block Plans ROMEO-01-PL02 25.11.2025\", to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rIf the approved waste storage and recycling facilities are not implemented within four months of the date of this decision, the occupation of the development shall cease until such time as details approved by the local planning authority have been implemented. Upon implementation, the approved enclosures and facilities specified in this condition shall be permanently retained. In the event of a legal challenge to this decision, or to a decision made pursuant to the procedure set out in this condition, the operation of the time limits specified in this condition shall be suspended until that legal challenge has been finally determined.\r\rReason: To ensure that sufficient provision at all times for the storage and collection of waste.\r"
  ],
